* A byte immediate known only later (a difference of labels further on, an equate further on)
* in andi, ori, cmpi, addi .b, or.b (ori.b), to ccr: the whole value as the extension word, as
* both Microware assemblers write it ($FFFE for -2; checked 2026-10-15 with Ultra C's r68);
* before, gas wrote only its low byte ($00FE). move.b keeps $00FE, as in both; a bit number is
* the same either way (0 to 31).
* fixed: bfaa6ae 2026-10-15 r68togas, rof2elf: -a= regression fix, later byte immediates, old libgen layout, ucc95 vsects; "gas" for GNU as
* expect text: 0200fffe 02010002 0002fffd 0c28fffd0004 023cfffe 08d10002 0604fffe 0006fffe 1e3c00fe 4e71 4e71 4e71
 psect byte_imm_later,0,0,0,0,0
 andi.b #Lab_a-Lab_b,d0
 andi.b #Lab_b-Lab_a,d1
 ori.b #Val_a,d2
 cmpi.b #Val_a,4(a0)
 andi #Lab_a-Lab_b,ccr
 bset #Lab_b-Lab_a,(a1)
 addi.b #Lab_a-Lab_b,d4
 or.b #Lab_a-Lab_b,d6
 move.b #Lab_a-Lab_b,d7
Lab_a
 nop
Lab_b
 nop
Val_a equ -3
 ends
